-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 26: REGISTRY AND ADMINISTRATION (rules 1 to 6; rule 5(2) is machinery), layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc6-order-23.l4.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a condition introduced by "if", "unless" or "except", a flat
--                negative ("must not be taken out"), or a time fixed in the text's own words and missed.
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it is silent on what follows a failure to comply with a "must", or a grant
--                ("may") is limited by its own wording and the case is outside the limit.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Order 26, Rule 1 (the Registry's departments, the Registrar's control, the Chief Executive) names which office directs, receives
-- reports and appoints: the functions below return the office the text names.
-- Order 26, Rule 5(2) (opening hours as directed by the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge) is machinery: the text gives no
-- hours and no fact to ask, so it has no function here (NOTES.md says so).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 26 -- Registry and administration`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- Registry of Supreme Court and of State Courts`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts (as the case may be)": the Chief Justice for the Registry of the
-- Supreme Court and the Presiding Judge of the State Courts for the Registry of the State Courts.
DECLARE `o 26 r 1 office` IS ONE OF
    `o 26 r 1 the Chief Justice`
    `o 26 r 1 the Presiding Judge of the State Courts`
    `o 26 r 1 someone else`
-- src:4053 | 1. —(1) There is a Registry with such departments and functions as the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts (as the case may be) may direct. (2) The Registry is under the control and supervision of the Registrar who must report to and be responsible to the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts (as the case may be) for its proper administration and functions.
@ref O 26 r 1(1) (src:4053)
GIVEN establishment IS A `Court system`
GIVETH A `o 26 r 1 office`
`o 26 r 1(1) the office that directs the departments and functions of the Registry` MEANS
    CONSIDER establishment
    WHEN `Supreme Court` THEN `o 26 r 1 the Chief Justice`
    WHEN `State Courts` THEN `o 26 r 1 the Presiding Judge of the State Courts`
@ref O 26 r 1(2) (src:4053)
GIVEN establishment IS A `Court system`
GIVETH A `o 26 r 1 office`
`o 26 r 1(2) the office to whom the Registrar must report and be responsible for the proper administration and functions of the Registry` MEANS
    CONSIDER establishment
    WHEN `Supreme Court` THEN `o 26 r 1 the Chief Justice`
    WHEN `State Courts` THEN `o 26 r 1 the Presiding Judge of the State Courts`
-- src:4054 | (3) The Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts (as the case may be) may appoint a Chief Executive and one or more Assistant Chief Executives to manage such functions of the Registry as he or she may direct, and they must report to and be responsible to the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts (as the case may be) for the proper discharge of those functions.
@ref O 26 r 1(3) (src:4054)
GIVEN establishment IS A `Court system`
      office IS A `o 26 r 1 office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 1(3) the office may appoint a Chief Executive and one or more Assistant Chief Executives` MEANS
    CONSIDER establishment
    WHEN `Supreme Court` THEN
        IF office EQUALS `o 26 r 1 the Chief Justice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts (as the case may be) may appoint": the power is the office's for its own Registry, and the paragraph does not say that another office may not
    WHEN `State Courts` THEN
        IF office EQUALS `o 26 r 1 the Presiding Judge of the State Courts`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts (as the case may be) may appoint": the power is the office's for its own Registry, and the paragraph does not say that another office may not
@ref O 26 r 1(3) (src:4054)
GIVEN establishment IS A `Court system`
GIVETH A `o 26 r 1 office`
`o 26 r 1(3) the office to whom the Chief Executive and the Assistant Chief Executives must report and be responsible for the proper discharge of the functions they manage` MEANS
    CONSIDER establishment
    WHEN `Supreme Court` THEN `o 26 r 1 the Chief Justice`
    WHEN `State Courts` THEN `o 26 r 1 the Presiding Judge of the State Courts`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- Practice directions`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- O 1 r 3(1) "practice directions" asks this function (the keel's `o 1 r 3(1) directions are practice directions` takes its answer as the input
-- `o 26 r 2 the directions are issued under Order 26, Rule 2`).  The approval needed is that of the Chief Justice for the Supreme
-- Court and that of the Presiding Judge of the State Courts for the State Courts ("as the case may be").
-- src:4056 | 2. The Registrar may issue practice directions from time to time with the approval of the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, as the case may be.
@ref O 26 r 2 (src:4056)
GIVEN issuer IS A `Court system`
      `the Registrar issued the directions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice approved them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Presiding Judge of the State Courts approved them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 2 the directions are issued under Order 26, Rule 2` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Registrar issued the directions`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may issue practice directions"
    ELSE
        CONSIDER issuer
        WHEN `Supreme Court` THEN
            IF `the Chief Justice approved them`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the approval of the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, as the case may be"
        WHEN `State Courts` THEN
            IF `the Presiding Judge of the State Courts approved them`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the approval of the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, as the case may be"

