§§ `Rule 3 -- Registry records`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4058 | 3. —(1) The Registry must maintain such Court records and other documents that are required by any written law or which the Registrar considers appropriate. (2) The Registry may collect, use or disclose such data which the Registrar considers appropriate.
@ref O 26 r 3(1) (src:4058)
GIVEN `the records and documents are required by a written law or the Registrar considers them appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registry maintains them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 3(1) the Registry maintains the Court records and other documents` MEANS
    IF `the records and documents are required by a written law or the Registrar considers them appropriate` AND `the Registry maintains them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the Registry "must maintain" them and does not say what follows if it does not

@ref O 26 r 3(2) (src:4058)
GIVEN `the Registrar considers the data appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 3(2) the Registry may collect, use or disclose the data` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar considers the data appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such data which the Registrar considers appropriate"

DECLARE `o 26 r 3(3) matter` IS ONE OF
    `o 26 r 3(3) the method of collection`
    `o 26 r 3(3) the storage`
    `o 26 r 3(3) the period of storage`
    `o 26 r 3(3) some other matter`

-- src:4059 | (3) The method of collection, the storage and the period of storage of Court records, documents and data are in the discretion of the Registrar.
@ref O 26 r 3(3) (src:4059)
GIVEN matter IS A `o 26 r 3(3) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 3(3) the matter is in the discretion of the Registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `o 26 r 3(3) the method of collection` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 26 r 3(3) the storage` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 26 r 3(3) the period of storage` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 26 r 3(3) some other matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names the method of collection, the storage and the period of storage of Court records, documents and data

-- src:4060 | (4) The Registrar may allow any person to search for, inspect and take a copy of any document filed in Court in any action if that person — ( a )
-- src:4061 | shows a valid interest in the document in question; and
