GIVEN `the redaction is in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 3(5) the Registrar may redact the document before a person searches for, inspects or takes a copy of it` MEANS
    IF `the redaction is in the interests of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the interests of justice"

-- src:4065 | (6) Documents filed in Court in any action and the Registry’s records must not be taken out of the Registry without the Registrar’s approval.
@ref O 26 r 3(6) (src:4065)
GIVEN `the Registrar approved taking the document or record out of the Registry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 3(6) the document or record may be taken out of the Registry` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar approved taking the document or record out of the Registry`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph bars taking it out "without the Registrar's approval" and does not say that it may be taken out with approval
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be taken out of the Registry without the Registrar's approval"

-- src:4066 | (7) Documents filed in Court must be typewritten and printed and must comply with practice directions relating to quality and dimensions of paper, font size, print quality, margins, copies and any other requirements.
@ref O 26 r 3(7) (src:4066)
GIVEN `the document is typewritten and printed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document complies with the practice directions on quality and dimensions of paper, font size, print quality, margins, copies and any other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 3(7) the document filed in Court is typewritten, printed and complies with the practice directions` MEANS
    IF `the document is typewritten and printed` AND `the document complies with the practice directions on quality and dimensions of paper, font size, print quality, margins, copies and any other requirements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says documents "must be typewritten and printed and must comply" and does not say what follows if they do not

