      `the service enables a subscriber to search for, inspect and take a copy of the documents filed in the Registry that the Registrar determines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 3(8) the Registrar may authorise a person to provide the service` MEANS
    IF `the service enables a subscriber to search the information relating to Court records and other documents that the Registrar determines` AND `the service enables a subscriber to search for, inspect and take a copy of the documents filed in the Registry that the Registrar determines`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- (a) "; and" (b): the service the Registrar may authorise is one that enables a subscriber to do both
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a service that enables a subscriber of that service — (a) ...; and (b) ..."

-- src:4071 | (9) The person authorised to provide the service mentioned in paragraph (8) must pay to the Registrar such fees for that service to have access to the information and documents mentioned in paragraph (8)( a ) and ( b ), as may be agreed between the Registrar and that person.
