@ref O 26 r 3(10) (src:4072-4075)
GIVEN `the service is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      what IS A `o 26 r 3(10) what the subscriber does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 3(10) the subscriber may do this without paying the prescribed fee and without the Registrar's permission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the service is in operation`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "at any time when that service is in operation"
        IF what EQUALS `o 26 r 3(10)(a) search the information mentioned in paragraph (8)(a)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF what EQUALS `o 26 r 3(10)(b) search for, inspect or take a copy of a document mentioned in paragraph (8)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subscriber is entitled to the two things named

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- Filing of powers of attorney`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 26 r 4(1)(a) how the execution of the document is verified` IS ONE OF
    `o 26 r 4(1)(a)(i) an affidavit or a statutory declaration made by a witness to the execution or by an impartial person who knows the signature of the donor`
    `o 26 r 4(1)(a)(ii) the signature of a commissioner for oaths as a witness to the execution`
    `o 26 r 4(1)(a)(iii) such other evidence which is satisfactory to the Registrar`
    `o 26 r 4(1)(a) in none of these ways`

-- src:4077 | 4. —(1) A document or a certified copy of a document creating a power of attorney may be deposited in the Registry of the Supreme Court under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act if — ( a )
-- src:4078 | the execution of the document is verified by — (i)
-- src:4079 | an affidavit or a statutory declaration made by a witness to the execution or by an impartial person who knows the signature of the donor of the power of attorney;
-- src:4080 | (ii)
-- src:4081 | the signature of a commissioner for oaths as a witness to the execution; or
-- src:4082 | (iii)
-- src:4083 | such other evidence which is satisfactory to the Registrar;
-- src:4084 | ( b )
-- src:4085 | the document is accompanied by the affidavit, statutory declaration, certificate or other evidence by which the execution was verified; and
-- src:4086 | ( c )
-- src:4087 | in the case of a certified copy of the document, the signature of the person who verified the copy is sufficiently verified.
@ref O 26 r 4(1) (src:4077-4087)
GIVEN verification IS A `o 26 r 4(1)(a) how the execution of the document is verified`
      `the document is accompanied by the affidavit, statutory declaration, certificate or other evidence by which the execution was verified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document deposited is a certified copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature of the person who verified the copy is sufficiently verified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 4(1) the document creating a power of attorney may be deposited in the Registry of the Supreme Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF verification EQUALS `o 26 r 4(1)(a) in none of these ways` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if — (a) the execution of the document is verified by — (i) ...; (ii) ...; or (iii) ..."
        IF (NOT `the document is accompanied by the affidavit, statutory declaration, certificate or other evidence by which the execution was verified`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (b) the document is accompanied by the affidavit, statutory declaration, certificate or other evidence by which the execution was verified"
        IF `the document deposited is a certified copy` AND (NOT `the signature of the person who verified the copy is sufficiently verified`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (c) in the case of a certified copy of the document, the signature of the person who verified the copy is sufficiently verified"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref O 26 r 4(1) (src:4077)
`o 26 r 4(1) the Registry in which the document creating a power of attorney may be deposited` MEANS "the Registry of the Supreme Court"
-- src:4088 | (2) The Registry of the Supreme Court must maintain an index of all documents or certified copies of documents creating a power of attorney that are deposited and of the names of the donors.
@ref O 26 r 4(2) (src:4088)
GIVEN `the Registry maintains an index of all the documents deposited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the index includes the names of the donors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 4(2) the Registry of the Supreme Court maintains the index` MEANS
    IF `the Registry maintains an index of all the documents deposited` AND `the index includes the names of the donors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the Registry "must maintain" the index and does not say what follows if it does not

DECLARE `o 26 r 4(3) what the person may do` IS ONE OF
    `o 26 r 4(3)(a) search the index mentioned in paragraph (2)`
    `o 26 r 4(3)(b) inspect a document filed or deposited in the Registry in accordance with paragraph (1)`
    `o 26 r 4(3)(c) be supplied with a copy or a certified copy of such a document`
    `o 26 r 4(3) something else`

