        IF what EQUALS `o 26 r 4(3) something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement is to the three things named
        IF `the person pays the prescribed fee` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on payment of the prescribed fee"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 5 -- Registry hours`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4096 | 5. —(1) The Registry must be open on every day of the year except non‑court days. (2) The Registry’s opening hours are as directed by the Chief Justice or the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, as the case may be.
@ref O 26 r 5(1) (src:4096)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Court calendar`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 5(1) the Registry must be open on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 1 r 3(1) a day is a non-court day` day calendar
    WHEN JUST nonCourt THEN
        IF nonCourt
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on every day of the year except non‑court days"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the non-court day answer is not available

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 6 -- Court vacations`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4098 | 6. There must be a Judge available during the Court vacations to hear such matters as the Registrar considers urgent.
@ref O 26 r 6 (src:4098)
GIVEN `it is during the Court vacations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar considers the matter urgent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Judge is available to hear the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 26 r 6 a Judge is available during the Court vacations to hear the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it is during the Court vacations`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a), "during" a period the text names: assumed, see F-ASSUMED): "There must be a Judge available during the Court vacations"
        IF (NOT `the Registrar considers the matter urgent`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to hear such matters as the Registrar considers urgent" is a scope limit with no "only"
        IF `a Judge is available to hear the matter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule says there "must be" a Judge available and does not say what follows if there is not (listed in F-MUST)
